counterfactuals.output:
A method for optically reading a microfluidic microplate, the method comprising:

providing a microfluidic microplate comprising a plurality of microfluidic cells, each microfluidic cell including a loading well configured to receive a liquid sample, a central base aperture disposed below or adjacent a base region of the loading well, a spiral microchannel in fluid communication with the loading well and extending radially about the central base aperture, and an outlet hole fluidically coupled to an end portion of the spiral microchannel;

introducing the liquid sample into the loading well of at least one of the microfluidic cells, whereby the liquid sample is advanced from the loading well through the spiral microchannel toward the outlet hole;

positioning the microfluidic microplate relative to an optical reading system comprising at least one illumination beam and at least one optical detector;

targeting the illumination beam at an off-center read location of the microfluidic cell, the off-center read location being laterally displaced from a geometric center of the loading well and laterally displaced from the central base aperture, such that the illumination beam interrogates a selected portion of the spiral microchannel rather than passing directly through the central base aperture;

directing the illumination beam through or onto the selected portion of the spiral microchannel containing the liquid sample;

collecting optical radiation from the selected portion of the spiral microchannel, the collected optical radiation comprising at least one of transmitted radiation, reflected radiation, scattered radiation, fluorescent radiation, luminescent radiation, or absorbance-related radiation; and

determining, from the collected optical radiation, at least one optical characteristic of the liquid sample within the spiral microchannel.

In one implementation, the off-center read location is selected to avoid optical interference caused by the central base aperture, the loading well, or meniscus effects in the loading well. In another implementation, the optical reading system reads a plurality of the microfluidic cells by sequentially aligning the illumination beam with respective off-center read locations corresponding to spiral microchannels of the plurality of microfluidic cells.
